<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahmud II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahmud II was Ottoman sultan from 1808 to 1839. He centralised the empire, destroying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> corps in 1826 and breaking the power of provincial notables such as the Bushati pashas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Scutari</a> in 1831. His reign also saw Greek independence and the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahmud-ii.jpg" alt="Mahmud II" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Guillaume Schlesinger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahmud_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
